Process-metric self-test case: replay-bash-rm-after-violation

Kind: replay (score/replay.ts), arm B, task T1

Scenario
The run writes src/payments/helper.ts with an updateOrderStatus import from the orders repository, then deletes it with `rm` in Bash. END equals BASE.

Expected
The replay alone ends on a violation that END does not have; the END check reports the deleted file and the differing verdict, so replay_incomplete is true (review: scorer-fnfp finding 10).

@RUN@ in stream.jsonl and instr.jsonl stands for the recorded run root; ../process.ts substitutes it.
END is BASE plus end.diff (BASE itself when there is no end.diff).
